# LOAD-BEARING: this is the TOC the Forever client actually loads.
#
# Measured on Forever beta build 70338: the client (game type "camelot") reads
# PadleyUI_Camelot.toc. The documented "_Forever" alias was NOT honoured - with
# only PadleyUI_Forever.toc present the addon vanished from the addon list.
# Keep both files with distinct X-PadleyUI-TOC values; the probe records the
# one actually read as build.tocVariant. Keep their file lists identical.
#
# Retail (game type "standard") reads neither file and keeps using PadleyUI.toc.
# Do NOT add a _Mainline.toc: that family suffix would also be picked up by
# retail, ahead of the unsuffixed PadleyUI.toc.
#
# HAZARD: if no suffixed TOC matches the client's game type, WoW falls back to
# the unsuffixed PadleyUI.toc (Interface 120100).
#
# File list is identical to PadleyUI.toc's (TEMP probes included - they are
# read-only slash commands). Forever-specific behaviour hangs off ns.FLAVOR
# (Core\Constants.lua); skins that cannot work on Forever skip themselves
# inside Apply().

Core\Constants.lua
Core\RestoredRegions.lua
Core\Fonts.lua
Core\SkinEngine.lua
Core\Config.lua
Core\Movers.lua
Skins\DamageMeter.lua
Skins\Tooltip.lua
Skins\Loot.lua
Skins\GameMenu.lua
Skins\Chat.lua
Skins\StatusBar.lua
Skins\Minimap.lua
Skins\ActionBars.lua
Skins\CooldownTracker.lua
Skins\Nameplates.lua
Skins\CastBar.lua
Skins\GCDBar.lua
Skins\Items.lua
Skins\CharacterFrame.lua
Skins\UnitFrames.lua
Skins\ClassPower.lua
Skins\PartyFrames.lua
Skins\MirrorTimer.lua
Skins\BetterBags.lua
Skins\ObjectiveTracker.lua
Skins\Professions.lua
Skins\WorldMap.lua
Skins\ChatBubbles.lua
Skins\TimerTracker.lua
Skins\EncounterBar.lua
PadleyUI.lua

